\lispPackageChapter{chorus/driver-api}

This package is the foreign binding to the CUDA driver API. Names follow the
driver entry points with a \texttt{cu-} prefix and Lisp hyphens. When the
driver library is absent, a call signals \texttt{sdk-not-found-error}.

\section{Variables}

\lispVariableSubsection{*sdk-not-found*}

True when the driver library did not load.

\lispVariableSubsection{*show-messages*}

Controls driver-API diagnostic messages. \texttt{chorus} reexports both
variables.

\section{Types}

\texttt{cu-result}, \texttt{cu-device}, \texttt{cu-context},
\texttt{cu-module}, \texttt{cu-function}, \texttt{cu-stream},
\texttt{cu-event}, \texttt{cu-device-ptr}, and \texttt{size-t}.

\section{Event flags}

\texttt{cu-event-default}, \texttt{cu-event-blocking-sync},
\texttt{cu-event-disable-timing}, and \texttt{cu-event-interprocess}.

\section{Functions}

Device and context: \texttt{cu-init}, \texttt{cu-device-get},
\texttt{cu-device-get-count}, \texttt{cu-device-compute-capability},
\texttt{cu-device-get-attribute},
\texttt{cu-device-attribute-compute-capability-major},
\texttt{cu-device-attribute-compute-capability-minor},
\texttt{cu-device-get-name}, \texttt{cu-ctx-create},
\texttt{cu-ctx-destroy}, \texttt{cu-ctx-synchronize}, and
\texttt{cu-device-total-mem}.

Memory: \texttt{cu-mem-alloc}, \texttt{cu-mem-free},
\texttt{cu-mem-host-register}, \texttt{cu-mem-host-unregister},
\texttt{cu-memcpy-host-to-device}, \texttt{cu-memcpy-host-to-device-async},
\texttt{cu-memcpy-device-to-host}, and
\texttt{cu-memcpy-device-to-host-async}.

Modules and launch: \texttt{cu-module-load}, \texttt{cu-module-unload},
\texttt{cu-module-get-function}, \texttt{cu-module-get-global}, and
\texttt{cu-launch-kernel}.

Events: \texttt{cu-event-create}, \texttt{cu-event-destroy},
\texttt{cu-event-elapsed-time}, \texttt{cu-event-record}, and
\texttt{cu-event-synchronize}.

Streams: \texttt{cu-stream-create}, \texttt{cu-stream-destroy},
\texttt{cu-stream-query}, \texttt{cu-stream-synchronize}, and
\texttt{cu-stream-wait-event}.
